Hey guys, long-time lurker here.  If you're worried about being
spoiled, this message probably isn't for you.

So my fifty-thousandth Valkyrie named Shera looks like she might be in
shape for an ascension, which would be my first.  I've got the
candelabrum and the bell, I've found the vibrating square, and I'm
about to go grab the book.  I'm lv. 22, I've got max HP of 267, and AC
of -26.

I'm pretty paranoid about unleashing the Wizard.  I've carved a two
square wide tunnel through hell (connecting the upstairs and
downstairs of each level -- someone talked about doing this a long
time ago, and the advice stuck), and I'm thinking about turning around
and doing it through the main dungeon.  Would this be wise?  Or am I
just being crazy?

I have Mjollnir and GoP, I've been wearing a ring of searching and a
+3 ring of damage control and an Amulet of ESP (reflection from
Perseus' shield) People talk about rings of free action like they are
an essential part of every ascension, but I haven't been wearing one
and since I learned to not attack gelatenous cubes, I haven't been
paralyzed or anything like that.  Is there something bad waiting for
me if I don't have free action?

Standard Liches and Mindflayers are genocided, since those caused me
trouble the last time I made it to the castle.  The Master and Arch
varieties haven't been so bad. My worst moment actually came with a
demilich who was overly fond of his summon nasties spell.  With a good
ranged weapon and careful use of speed, they don't seem to cause too
many problems, especially with my Gehennom tunnel preventing me from
getting stuck in corners.  I've been cursed a couple of times, which
hasn't caused any real problems and my brains have been sucked once,
but I took screenshots of my knowledge of inventory before I entered
hell (is this cheating?) and the tunnels have made finding my way
around forgotten levels pretty easy.  Compared to the nastiness that
can happen in the mid-game, the most feared parts of Gehennom haven't
been rough at all.

Other resources at my disposal:
-blessed luckstone and unicorn horn, a lit magic lamp (before going
into gehennom i would have used it for a magic marker, but after
burning out 5 or 6 lamps and lanterns, this seemed like the way to go)
-two wands of death, one probably dry judging from how many times that
soldier used it.
-rings of levitation, conflict, free action, regeneration, polymorph
and polymorph control (is there anything that I maybe should change
into?  I guess I wouldn't be able to throw Mojo, but I'm game for
being a monster if it makes life easier.  I actually cleared the
castle primarily as a Jabberwok thanks to a poly trap) I haven't found
slow digestion, but I've got 30 K-Rations and I've kept myself fed
almost on trolls alone, so it hasn't been a problem.
-amulets of reflection and life saving (does Vlad's closet always have
one, or was I just lucky?  Also that guy needs to be a lot harder.  He
shot three arrows at me while I bounced mojo off of him.  Dragons are
more dangerous than that.)
-countless wands of magic missile, sleep, cold, fire, and lightning. 
I should ditch these, they're weighing me down, but I can't bring
myself to throw away a good wand.
-Sunsword and a +3 silver sabre.  I pull these out when something has
a wand that I don't want to blow up.
-One scroll of charging, a few remove curses, a few identifies, lots
of create monster scrolls and wands that i picked up to prevent
monsters from getting ahold of them

I haven't thought at all about my score, so I haven't bothered with
gems or the gold left over from my failed attempt to get protected
below 0.

So I guess I'm asking for advice on how to handle the ritual, the
wizard, and the planes.  Am I missing any significant items that I
should be seeking out before going on?  Are my HP and armor not good
enough?  Thus far Gehennom has been very very easy and I'm a little
overconfident.

And a note to players who, like me, just can't seem to ascend: slow
down, be patient, keep things like scrolls of teleport and wands of
digging handy, and be anal about things like gathering armor, not
drinking/reading unidentified things etc.  I've had *shitty* luck this
game, no pre-castle wishes, no magic markers, no scrolls of genocide
(two lucky throne-sits though), no bag of holding, 6 grey dragons and
no scales, only one scroll of enchant armor before the castle, a poly
trap in minesend that gave me a black dragon, a master lich, and a
master mind flayer before I could push a boulder on it, and despite
all of this (and some really stupid
walk-into-the-lava-with-no-levitation type moments) this has been my
best game ever, because I took it slow.

Also one last question: I've been playing this game at several
different computers, emailing my savegame back and forth.  If I die, I
plan on loading up a recent copy and finishing the game in explore
mode.  Would this be considered scumming? I really think this should
be a game feature.  If you die, you should have the option of
continuing in explore mode (seeing your score, but not your inventory)

Also if I make it back to dlvl 1, I'm probably going to make a nearly
identical character in wizmode to practice the elemental planes a
couple of times.

